[[Lok Lambert]] used Darkfog to obscure [[Rassimov]]'s vision of the Casterwill Compound's gate, in [[Atlantis]], allowing Lok to invoke [[Lindorm]] and attack an unsuspecting Rassimov. The spell [[Hexkill]] was used by Rassimov to counter Lok's spell, but it was too late. {{Source|Coming of Age}}

On the [[Huntik Foundation|Huntik]] team's way to the [[Golden Asp]], Darkfog was cast by [[Zhalia Moon]] to prevent two [[The Organization|Organization]] [[Suits]] who were following them from seeing Lok Lambert's [[Bristlebind]] spell, making their car bump into the vines and flip multiple times. {{Source|The Golden Asp}}

At the roof of [[Dante Vale's house]], Lok Lambert used this spell again to obscure [[Simon Judeau]]'s vision while trying to sneak up on him. However, Simon was still able to grab Lok through the spell. {{Source|The Secret of Two Generations}}

During the final battle against [[Simon Judeau|the Professor]], Lok Lambert momentarily blocked [[Tao]]'s vision with Darkfog, allowing [[Gar-Ghoul]] and [[Ariel]] to attack it. The spell later dissipated, letting the [[Legendary Titan]] sweep off Gar-Ghoul and send a faraway [[Ignatius]] back to its amulet. {{Source|The Mission}}

In the coast of Northern England, Lok Lambert used this spell to cover up the Huntik team's exit into the cliffs from the beach when they were attacked by three Organization Suits. {{Source|Knight of the Willblade}}

[[Tantras]] cast Darkfog at the [[Erasmus Bridge]] to allow him and his recruits to escape after the battle for Vigilante's amulet turned the Huntik team's way. {{Source|Den vs Harrison}}

Darkfog was once again used by Tantras to retreat with his new students after noticing [[Lindorm|Powerbonded Lindorm]] in the streets of [[Venice, Italy]]. {{Source|Boys Will Be Seekers}}

Dante Vale cast this spell when fighting [[Wind]] hand-to-hand to obscure his vision and help a troubled Lok Lambert and [[Sophie Casterwill]] inside the [[Phoenix Volcano]]. However, Wind reacted quickly and knocked down Dante with a spell of his own through Darkfog. {{Source|The Phoenix's Ashes}}

Darkfog was cast by [[Harrison Fears]] to sneakily take out a group of Organization personnel at the entrance of the [[Tomb of Tutankhamun]]. {{Source|Rassimov's Secret}}

